You are designing a soccer strategy. Your goal is to win the match by
scoring more goals than the opposing team within the allotted ticks.
The strategy is implemented as a Python function called decide(), which
the simulation invokes once per tick for each player on your team. The
function returns a single Action (Move, Pass, Shoot, Tackle, or Hold)
based on the current game state. The same function must work for both
teams, in any roster size, on any field dimensions.

