# Example structure only — adapt for your team's strategy:
def decide(game_state, player_state, history):
    if player_state["has_ball"]:
        if player_state["role"] == "FWD":
            return Shoot(angle=0.0, power=15)
        return Pass(target_pos=(80.0, 30.0), power=12)
    return Move(dx=1.0, dy=0.0, speed=1.0)

=== SECTION 7: FIELD GEOMETRY ===
Field and goal geometry vary by config — read every value from inputs:
  game_state["field"]["width"]            # field width
  game_state["field"]["height"]           # field height
  game_state["field"]["team_a_goal_x"]    # x-coord of team_a's defending goal
  game_state["field"]["team_b_goal_x"]    # x-coord of team_b's defending goal
  game_state["field"]["goal_top"]         # larger-y edge of the goal mouth (numerically GREATER, e.g. 33.66)
  game_state["field"]["goal_bottom"]      # smaller-y edge of the goal mouth (numerically LESS, e.g. 26.34)
# Convention: goal_top > goal_bottom. The mouth spans y in [goal_bottom, goal_top].
# Goal-mouth height is (goal_top - goal_bottom) and is POSITIVE — never write
# (goal_bottom - goal_top); it is negative and silently breaks shot/aim gates.
# Use abs(goal_top - goal_bottom) for the size and (goal_top + goal_bottom)/2 for the center y.
Pick your defending goal from the field by team: team_a → field["team_a_goal_x"],
team_b → field["team_b_goal_x"]; you attack the OPPOSITE goal. These x-values SWAP at
half-time — read them every tick. Never assume team_a attacks +x or any fixed direction.
Never hardcode 100×60 or any specific coordinate.

=== SECTION 8: ACTION SPACE ===
5 action types: Move(dx, dy, speed), Pass(target_pos, power), Shoot(angle, power), Tackle(target_player_id), Hold().
Validation: non-carrier Pass/Shoot → Hold(); out-of-range Tackle → Hold(); speed clamped to [0, 1].

OFFSIDE (IFAB Law 11, judged on the x-axis at the moment a team-mate PASSES):
a team-mate is in an offside position if they are strictly inside the
opponents' half AND strictly nearer the opponents' goal line than both the
ball and the second-last opponent (any role — usually GK + last defender).
Level with the second-last opponent = onside. If a player who was in an
offside position when the pass was struck is the FIRST to control that pass,
play stops: free kick to the opposing team at that spot (possession lost).
No offside from goal kicks, throw-ins, or corner kicks.
Tactics: attackers — time runs to stay level with the last defender until
the pass is struck, then sprint. Passers — check the receiver is onside
BEFORE passing forward. Defenders — hold a coordinated high line to trap
goal-hangers.

FOULS AND CARDS (IFAB Law 12): every Tackle attempt risks a foul — the
chance scales with your `offensive` rating. A foul stops play: direct free
kick to the fouled team (your team must retreat 9.15 from the ball), or a
PENALTY KICK if the foul happened inside your own penalty area (within
16.5 of your goal line). Foul severity may bring a yellow card (reckless)
or a straight red (excessive force). A red card — or two yellows — sends
the player off for the REST OF THE MATCH with no replacement.
Tactics: never tackle inside your own penalty area unless the alternative
is a near-certain goal. Check player_state["yellow_cards"] — on 1 yellow,
prefer containment (shadowing the carrier with Move) over tackling.

FREE-KICK TAKING (Law 13): when game_state["free_kick_kicker"] equals your
my_player_id, you are taking a free kick — the ball is not in play until
you kick it. You MUST Pass or Shoot (Hold to wait is allowed); Move is
blocked. Opponents cannot tackle you until the kick. If you stall ~2s the
engine auto-passes to your nearest teammate — better to pick a target
yourself.

=== SECTION 9: ATTRIBUTE REFERENCE ===
11 attributes (range 1-20):
  speed: maximum movement per tick.
  skill: ball control under pressure + tackle/save fallback.
  strength: tackle outcome + max kick power.
  save: GK-only; goal-line save radius.
  discipline: how strongly the formation snap pulls the player back when idle.
    SOFT — at most 20% of motion. Active intent (Move at speed >= 0.5, or
    any carrier action) bypasses snap entirely.
  dribbling: success rate when carrying the ball past a defender.
  passing: pass landing accuracy. Effective skill in pass formula =
    (2 * passing + skill) / 3 — specialist dominates, skill cushions.
  shooting: shot angular accuracy. Same blend with skill as passing.
  stamina: endurance. Each non-Hold action drains current_health by
    base_cost × (1 - stamina/20). stamina=20 burns no health.
    All success formulas multiply by health_factor = 0.6 + 0.4 ×
    current_health/100, so a tired player is 60-100% as effective.
    Hold and low-speed Move recover health; half-time restores fully.
  offensive: aggression (IFAB Law 12 trade-off). High offensive boosts
    tackle effectiveness (±15% at the extremes) BUT raises foul chance
    proportionally (foul risk doubles at 20, vanishes near 1). See the
    FOULS AND CARDS rules in SECTION 8.
  penalty: penalty-kick conversion. The engine auto-selects the on-field
    team-mate with the highest penalty rating to take an awarded penalty;
    conversion probability rises with the rating and falls against a
    keeper with a high save rating.

Role tactical guidance (phase-aware — see SECTION 11):
  GK : stays in penalty area; saves shots; clears with Pass.
  DEF: holds shape when team_phase=defending; PUSHES UP toward midfield
       when team_phase=attacking. Overlapping runs encouraged when team
       has sustained possession in opponent's half.
  MID: shuttles between thirds based on team_phase. Supports both
       attack and defense. The most position-flexible role.
  FWD: presses high when team_phase=attacking; drops back to support
       press / mid-third recovery when team_phase=defending.

